Pragmatic: replace the stream-factory assertions with a direct call of the chain-building seam: `resolver.chainFor('default')` — protected? It's `List<ChainEntry>? chainFor(String role)` — public (line 145). ChainEntry fields: model, keyRing, streamForKey — public. So:

```dart
final entries = resolver.chainFor('default')!;
expect(entries, hasLength(1));
expect(entries.single.model.provider, 'anthropic');
// the keyless entry's credential is the EMPTY sentinel — the stream
// factory receives '' (byte-parity with the non-roles keyless boot)
final key = entries.single.keyRing.currentCredential.value;
expect(key, '');
```

And verify streamForKey('') returns a function without touching the factory? It returns the routed stream function — calling streamForKey('') itself triggers `buildRouted()` → `_streamFactory(spec.kind, currentKey)` — that DOES invoke the factory with currentKey ('')! So:

```dart
final streamFn = entries.single.streamForKey('');
expect(seenKind, 'anthropic');
expect(seenKey, '');
```

