The ring value is 'a-key' — the resolver fell back to the provider's env name despite keyless. Why? `_keyBaseName(ref, spec)`: `ref.apiKeyName` null → endpoint-scoped → null (localhost vs anthropic default? `sameEndpoint('http://localhost:8080/v1', 'https://api.anthropic.com')` false → scopedName = FA_KEY_<host> for localhost → `collectKeyStack(_secrets, 'FA_KEY_LOCALHOST...')` empty → falls to `spec.apiKeyEnvNames` → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = 'a-key' → returns it. So keyBase != null → my keyless branch never runs (it only handles keyBase == null).

Fix: the keyless check must come FIRST — a keyless ref uses the empty ring regardless of any discoverable key:

```dart
final ring = ref.keyless
    ? ApiKeyRing(baseName: '', credentials: const [ApiKeyCredential('', '')])
    : _buildCredentialedRing(ref, spec, skipped);
if (ring == null) return null;
```

